text_en:
In response to the Japanese AMMTC leader’s criticism of the situation in Myanmar, the Union Minister said: 

- Regional interests can be achieved through peaceful coexistence without interference by another country in the internal affairs of an ASEAN member country; 

- This meeting is only to discuss the exchange of views on combating transnational crime in the ASEAN region and cooperation between the countries involved; 

- Myanmar’s developments are purely internal and not a regional issue, and will not be discussed at such regional meetings; 

- If there are any issues related to Myanmar’s politics that need to be discussed, the two countries can meet and discuss them separately, he said.

